<title>COLOMBIA: Banco de Colombia falls on announcement.</title>
<headline>Banco de Colombia falls on announcement.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of Banco de Colombia was temporarily suspended in Bogota and Medellin Friday after the bank's stock dropped sharply on news it had broken off plans to form a strategic partnership with Spain's Banco Central Hispano-Americano.</p>
<p>Traders in Bogota and Medellin said the bank's stock fell by about 10 percent to 361 pesos per share before trading was suspended for a 30-minute &quot;cooling off period.&quot;</p>
<p>The bank's stock has suffered all year from delays in completing the merger with BCH, which was first announced in mid-1996.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
